& [SemanticSubjectAudit] passes
  + the subject is one relation between two complete supplied canonical sequence commitments
  + scope comparability and digest equality remain distinct decisions
  + Equal and Different are ordinary dispositions only after both current-rederivation and scope gates pass
  + profile or scope mismatch is not inventory difference
  + operand order is retained provenance but not time order
  + correlation identities remain retained without becoming scope or equality content
  + physical origin, acquisition order, repetition, stability, completeness, quiescence, receipt, and admission are excluded

& [VocabularyAudit] passes
  + left and right are positional operand roles
  + comparable is a pure relation over profiles, limits, and root identity
  + equal and different concern only canonical sequence digest values
  + stable is reserved because stability requires an observed temporal relation absent here
  + before and after are reserved because physical acquisition order is absent
  + double_inventory is reserved for two proven physical acquisitions
  + quiescent_double_inventory additionally requires lifecycle and writer accounting
  - never: alias any reserved grade to supplied pair equality

& [ScopeAudit] passes subject to canonical restatement
  + current digest, encoding, retained-plan, and assembly profiles must be exact on both operands
  + exact complete TopologyScanLimits prevent silent comparison across distinct declared ceilings
  + root relative path, Directory kind, volume serial, and file identity define common root scope
  + changing other root observation fields is committed sequence difference rather than scope substitution
  + assembly, commitment, reconciliation, projection, and entry-reference identities are correlation or lineage roles
  + no minimum, maximum, union, intersection, default, normalization, or field repair is permitted

& [RederivationAudit] passes
  + WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigest derives Clone, PartialEq, and Eq
  + immutable getters expose its retained plan and complete assembly
  + both retained values derive Clone and may be passed to the proven public digest transform
  + exact complete result equality detects any contradiction between supplied and current pure derivation
  + the reconciliation module need not access private fields or duplicate the canonical writer
  + side-qualified nested digest faults preserve exact failure provenance

& [DispositionAudit] passes
  + digest values are already validated lowercase 64-hex outputs of the prerequisite transform
  + byte string equality under exact common encoding profile is sufficient for the selected supplied equality relation, subject to ordinary SHA-256 collision assumptions
  + Different is expected evidence and must not be converted into a fault
  + a closed named enum is semantically clearer than bool
  + no changed-field or causal explanation is authorized

& [DataDesignAudit] passes
  + conceptual subject is a comparable supplied digest pair
  + logical representation is plan, two complete operands, one common-scope record, and one disposition
  + physical representation is bounded in-memory Rust values with no canonical-byte or filesystem state
  + ownership is by-value at release and clone-only during pre-release current rederivation
  + lineage representation retains both complete output-only prerequisite carriers
  + compatibility is exact-profile and additive with no migration or default

& [ImplementationFeasibility] is dependency ready
  + cantor_ecosystem already owns both prerequisite modules and serde
  + no SHA-256 operation is added because reconciliation compares validated prerequisite outputs
  + TopologyScanLimits and all required root fields implement exact equality
  + the first assembly member and topology observation are accessible through immutable getters
  + safe Rust cloning, validation, comparison, and construction are sufficient
  + zero unsafe, platform, filesystem, clock, or other effect calls are needed

& [ConstraintAudit] identifies canonical obligations
  + restate the exact two-carrier input and reject every lower overload
  + define side-specific rederivation order and fault precedence
  + define profile, limits, and root-scope comparison order
  + distinguish scope fault from Different disposition
  + state exactly which root fields are identity scope and which remain committed mutable content
  + require both complete operands and common scope to be retained
  + prohibit temporal vocabulary and physical-grade inference in code, tests, docs, and evidence

& [RiskAudit] is bounded
  + [highest_risk] supplied Equal could be rhetorically inflated into stable physical double inventory
  + [second_risk] bare digest comparison could sever output-only proof lineage
  + [third_risk] unequal limits or different roots could be misclassified as ordinary inventory drift
  + [fourth_risk] a duplicated canonical encoder could drift from the prerequisite authority
  + closed vocabulary, output-only inputs, current rederivation, exact scope faults, and static boundary checks address these risks

& [EffectAudit] passes
  + required implementation is deterministic in-memory cloning, rederivation, validation, comparison, and result construction only
  + filesystem, Windows, handle, process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, database, Git, model, tool, fixture, mutation, seal, test-execution effect, cleanup, and promotion authority remain absent
  + physical scanning and all locked effect paths remain locked

